  <h2 style="margin-top: 50px;">Letter From the Director of Graduate Studies in Sociology</h2>

  <div class="two-column" style="margin-top: 30px;">
    <div class="column" style="width: 35%;">
      <img src="" alt="Profile" class="profile-image">
      <div class="signature-block">
        <div style="font-weight: bold;">Dr. {{ director_name }}</div>
        <div>{{ director_title }}</div>
        <div>{{ director_department }}</div>
        <div>{{ director_specialty }}</div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="column" style="width: 65%;">
      <div class="body-text">
        <p>Welcome to the Fall {{ year }} issue of DuBois Courier. The newsletter is named in honor of one of the most important sociologists in the late 19th century and much of the 20th century. His work on race and religion continue to impact sociology and other disciplines.</p>
        <p>Here we are at the start of another semester. Welcome back graduate faculty and returning students! Please join me in welcoming first year students: {{ student_name_1 }}, {{ student_name_2 }}, {{ student_name_3 }}, {{ student_name_4 }}, {{ student_name_5 }}, {{ student_name_6 }}, and {{ student_name_7 }}.</p>
        <p>Congratulations to everyone who reached various milestones in the PhD program and to Dr. {{ faculty_name_1 }} for his promotion from associate professor to full professor. Special congratulations to recent graduates: Dr. {{ grad_name_1 }}, Dr. {{ grad_name_2 }}, and Dr. {{ grad_name_3 }}!</p>
        <p>Our students and faculty are producing new knowledge and sharing that knowledge in academic books and peer-reviewed journals, and at professional conferences. Selected publications by faculty and graduate students are listed in the current issue. Also in the current issue, learn more about Dr. {{ faculty_name_2 }} in the Faculty Spotlight and {{ faculty_name_3 }} in the Graduate Student Spotlight.</p>
        <p>Great things are happening in the Department of Sociology. Let's build on the momentum!</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="page">
  <div class="section-heading">CHAIR'S CORNER</div>
  <div style="margin-bottom: 20px;">
    <div style="font-weight: bold;">Department Chair – {{ chair_name }}</div>
    <div>Professor, Sociology</div>
  </div>

  <div class="two-column" style="margin-top: 20px;">
    <div class="column" style="width: 35%;">
      <img src="" alt="Profile" class="profile-image">
    </div>
    <div class="column" style="width: 65%;">
      <div class="body-text">
        <p>Hi from {{ location_1 }} where I spend my summers. I am not the only one who was recently out of the country. {{ person_1 }} has been in {{ country_1 }} and {{ country_2 }}. {{ person_2 }} is in {{ country_3 }} and {{ country_4 }}. Our faculty members are all over the world, and some of our graduate students are in the same boat. {{ person_3 }} just came back from her stint in {{ city_1 }}, the United Arab Emirates. {{ person_4 }} was in {{ city_2 }}. (Excuse me if I missed anyone).</p>
        <p>While LSU Sociology faculty and students are spread out all over the world, we manage everyday endeavors: publications, presentations, and teaching. Amid numerous publications, I will just mention {{ person_5 }} (Dana Berkowitz), {{ person_6 }} (Shurum), and {{ person_7 }} (Lori Martin). I am also happy to report that {{ person_8 }} will be a full professor as of this August, and {{ person_9 }} and {{ person_10 }} are becoming the Director of African and African American Studies (2017-18).</p>
        <p>As for awards, Dr. {{ person_11 }} swept won 3rd place in the 2017 Association of Black Sociologists' graduate student paper competition. {{ person_12 }} received a prestigious LSU Dissertation Fellowship, and {{ person_13 }} received a Humane Studies Fellowship. As for faculty, we have too many grants and awards to list. Our staff members are joining the ride: {{ person_14 }}, {{ person_15 }}, {{ person_16 }}, and {{ person_17 }} received the 2016 LSU Foundation Staff Outstanding Service Award. (Again, my apology if I missed anyone).</p>
        <p>We now have an assistant professor, {{ person_18 }}, from {{ university_1 }}. Please help us welcome her to our department.</p>
        <p>Speaking of that, I welcome incoming graduate students to our program. They are from all over the country and world, from {{ country_a }}, {{ country_b }}, {{ country_c }}, {{ country_d }}, {{ country_e }}, {{ country_f }}, among others. Each "cohort" consists of 5-13 students and most of our students are funded as Teaching Assistants or Research Assistants.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

